From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:03:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] nvk/android: free the memory imported for a native buffer
 image

vk_android_import_anb() allocates a VkDeviceMemory for the gralloc buffer
of a VkNativeBufferANDROID image and stores it in vk_image::anb_memory.
Drivers that create their images with vk_image_create() free it in
vk_image_destroy(). NVK allocates and frees its images itself, so that
memory, with its imported BO and dma-buf reference, outlived every
Android swapchain image.

Free it in nvk_image_finish(), which also covers vkCreateImage() failing
after the import.

Fixes: b192c6927b0 ("nvk/android: Add support for ANDROID_native_buffer")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
index 52563a9e69b..44a8df56804 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_image.c
@@ -1248,6 +1248,17 @@ nvk_image_finish(struct nvk_device *dev, struct nvk_image *image,
 
    simple_mtx_destroy(&image->tiled_shadow_mutex);
 
+#ifdef VK_USE_PLATFORM_ANDROID_KHR
+   /* vk_android_import_anb() allocated this with vkCreateImage()'s
+    * allocator, which vkDestroyImage() gets again.
+    */
+   if (image->vk.anb_memory != VK_NULL_HANDLE) {
+      dev->vk.dispatch_table.FreeMemory(nvk_device_to_handle(dev),
+                                        image->vk.anb_memory, pAllocator);
+      image->vk.anb_memory = VK_NULL_HANDLE;
+   }
+#endif
+
    vk_image_finish(&image->vk);
 }
 
